2b:Tc57,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.raulji.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Gujarat","item":"https://www.raulji.com/gujarat/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Surat","item":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"Private Limited","item":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/private-limited-company-registration/"}]},{"@type":"Service","@id":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/private-limited-company-registration/#service","name":"Private Limited Company Registration in Surat","description":"Surat's diamond and textile trades were built on partnership firms, so a Private Limited Company here is usually a deliberate step up rather than a starting point. When it happens, the reason is normally external: an export buyer, a lender, or a brand ambition that the old structure cannot support.","url":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/private-limited-company-registration/","serviceType":"Private Limited Company Registration","provider":{"@id":"https://www.raulji.com/#organization"},"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Surat","containedInPlace":{"@type":"AdministrativeArea","name":"Surat district, Gujarat"}},"offers":{"@type":"Offer","priceCurrency":"INR","price":"9999","description":"One-time professional fee. Government filing fees and stamp duty are charged separately and vary by state and authorised capital.","url":"https://www.raulji.com/surat/private-limited-company-registration/"}},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Should a Surat diamond or textile firm convert to a Private Limited Company?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if the company is buying you something specific: an export buyer or lender that requires it, a consumer brand you intend to invest in, or genuine plans to raise equity. If the real concern is personal liability, an LLP achieves that while keeping the partner structure and costing far less to run each year. Converting to a company for the status alone is rarely worth the compliance it brings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do export buyers require a company rather than a partnership firm?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It varies by buyer, but the direction of travel is towards wanting a limited-liability entity, and a company is the form international counterparties and their banks recognise most easily. Some accept an LLP. Since you usually know which buyer prompted the question, the sensible step is to check their contracting requirement before choosing a structure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What changes about how money is handled after incorporating?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Quite a lot, and it is the part Surat family firms find hardest. A company's money is not the owners' money. Taking it out requires a formal route such as salary, dividend or board-approved fees, all of it recorded. Statutory audit applies from the first financial year regardless of turnover, so the books have to be kept properly from day one rather than reconstructed later."}}]}]}21:[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2b"}}],"$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34"]
